    "title": "Grace uses balanced attack to halt Huntington - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n46 minutes ago\nWINONA LAKE, Ind. (WANE) – Grace College, ranked no. 1 in the NAIA Coaches Poll, looked every bit the part of a top-ranked team on Wednesday, besting Crossroads League rival Huntington University 78-59 behind a balanced offensive attack.\nFive Lancers scored in double figures with Michael Wellman leading the way with 12 points and Ian Raasch 11. Blackhawk Christian graduate Gage Sefton, Carroll grad Cannen Houser, and Tyler Raasch each had 10 points, while Manchester High School graduate Gavin Betten chipped in with 8.\nChurubusco grad Jackson Paul was Huntington’s lone player in double figures with a game-high 20 points.\nGrace College improves to 9-0 overall and 3-0 in Crossroads League play. The Lancers’ next game is at Spring Arbor on Saturday at 3 pm.\nHuntington falls to 7-3 overall and 1-2 in the Crossroads League. USF’s next game is Saturday at home against Indiana Wesleyan at 3 pm.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
